  "label": "Land Grabbing Myth",
  "description": "The 'land grab' myth is a false narrative that claims immigrants are stealing land from native populations. This myth is often used to justify anti-immigrant policies and to incite fear and hostility toward immigrants. It is rooted in historical narratives of colonization and land ownership, and is used to reinforce the idea that immigrants are economic and cultural threats.",
